/**
Vector :
Header_File : # include <vector>
---------------------------------------
(i) Declaration -1  : vector<data_type> vec_name
        eg: vector<int> v;
        eg: vector <float> v;
        eg: similarly for bool,string,char,double
-------------------------------------------------
(ii) Initialization: vector<data_type> vec_name = {values}
    eg: vector <int> v = {1,2};
    eg: vector<bool> v = {true,false}
-----------------------------------------------------------
(iii) Declaration- 2: vector <int> v (size,val)
    eg: vector<int> v (1,0);
    bool : true (default)
    char : \0
    string : " "
==========================================================
Inserting:
(i)Method -1: vec_name.push_back(val) : insert at end
eg: v.push_back(10)
----------------------------------------------------------
(ii)Method - 2: vec_name.insert (iterator,val) : insert at any pos.
Random access
iterator : begin() // start
            end() // points  after last element
            begin() + 1 // second ele
eg: v.insert (v.begin() + 2, 40)
==========================================================
Accessing
(i)Method - 1: v[i]
    eg: v[0];
----------------------------------------------------------
(ii)Method - 2: v.at (index) 
    eg: v.at(3)
----------------------------------------------------------------
==========================================================
Deletion:
(i) Method - 1: vec_name. pop_back() // delete last ele
                eg: v = [1,2,3,4]
                v.pop_back() // [1,2,3]
----------------------------------------------------------
(ii) Method - 2: vec_name.erase (iterator)
                eg: iterator : begin (),end()
                    eg: v.erase (v.begin())
==========================================================
Searching:
(i) Find : vec_name.find(start_iterator,end_iterator,key)
    Returns iterator if found 
            else : v.end()
    eg: i = v.find(v.begin(),v.end() ,10)
        i --> pointer 
        *i --> value
        i - v.begin() --> index
==========================================================
Traversing:
for (auto i : v)
    cout<<i;
==========================================================
Other Functions:
(i) Size: v.size() // returns number of elements
(ii) empty() : v.empty() // returns 1 : true , 0 : false
==========================================================
2-D Vector:
vector<vector<int>v = {
                        {1,2},
                        {3,4}
                        }
(i)Traversing:
    for (auto i : v)
    {
    for (auto j : i)
    cout<<j
    }

    Method - 2:
    for (int i =0;i<v.size()i++)
    {
    for (int j = 0;j<v[0].size();j++)
    {
    cout<<V[i][j];
    }
    }
                                


